A||||9||Adrift||No cigarette lighter on my car...?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-22-2001||05:57 PM||||Well, As some of you may know I got my car without an interior, and have been slowy building it up - today I realized something - theres no cigarette lighter to plug in my cell phone or whatever! There are few wiring harness type things sitting the centre console not hooked up to anything, but I can't figure out how I'm going to get a cigarette lighter back! <BR>Here's a list of everything in my centre console:<P>Two power window switches<BR>one power mirror switch<BR>two lights<P>There are many wires not hooked into anything specific. What else am I missing?||||reg||1
Z||000001||cadaver||11-22-2001||06:17 PM||||The power window and mirror wiring comes from the front. The two wires for the cig lighter come from the back. One black and one orange I think.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-22-2001||07:38 PM||||Unless it's been cut, it comes from near the ECM. At the end of the lighter harness there should be 2 spade lugs for the lighter socket and a socket for the lighter lamp.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-22-2001||10:58 PM||||And somewhere in that mess of wires coming from the ECM area, there should be the ALDL, too.  The end of that will have a multi socketed plug. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Adrift||11-23-2001||11:27 AM||||Whats ALDL?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Adrift||11-23-2001||11:34 AM||||One other thing - is the cigarette lighter a standard plug? Can I just go to Canadian Tire or an auto parts store and buy a cigarette lighter and just plug it in?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||11-23-2001||03:55 PM||||I forget what ALDL stands for but it's what the mechanic plugs his device into so he can check your computer codes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||11-23-2001||09:27 PM||||Assembly Line Diagnostic Link||||reg||1
Z||000008||clayatandalusia||11-24-2001||01:39 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/</A>  has replacement cig adapt.. you auto parts store might have it ..  it has to screw holes to either side<BR>if you want used try kick hill farm ... thay have used parts there i cnat remember the addy search for it if you can find one e-mail me i have several..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||11-24-2001||01:24 PM||||I'll have to write this one up next I think. The lighter is simple and complicated at the same time. When you can see all the peices, it's pretty simple. If you can't, or worse have never in your life seen a whole one, then it can be pretty bloody annoying.<P>There are 4 main parts to Fiero's lighter.<P>The sleeve and socket are standard Casco parts available almost anywhere.<P>The Shell, which screws onto the sleeve to hold everything together, is standard Casco but has been modified for the lamp holder.<P>That I've seen... The light socket, which is of zilch benifit and no loss, only fits the factory lamp holder. I think Caso does have a lighted shell that can replace it if you really want it.<P>The 4th part is a metal plate that hold the assembled lighter socket to the plastic center console guts.<P>The lighter has also been moded with spade terminals. The + terminal screws to the center terminal of the socket. the other one, ground, is welded to the shell.<P><BR>The easiest way to fix this is find a complete Fiero compatble socket and, if need be, put new guts into it. Then you'll have all the correct parts. ||||reg||1
